  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chicken tikka masala separates into two steps: marinating the chicken, and building the sauce. The marinade step, yoghurt, lemon, and spices, gives the chicken its characteristic charred, spiced crust. Here, the marinated chicken goes into a hot pan to get some colour before joining the pressure-cooked sauce."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The tikka is the 'tikka', the spiced, browned chicken pieces. The masala is the sauce. Both need to be right. Marinating for at least one hour (overnight is better) and searing the pieces in a hot pan before the sauce goes into the pressure cooker makes the difference between a flat result and the version people return to."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A swirl of cream and a scattering of fresh coriander are optional but standard at the table."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
